  <processInformation>
    <dataSetInformation>
      <common:UUID>50d49173-7033-414c-b331-027baebd87b7</common:UUID>
      <name>
        <baseName xml:lang="en">Electricity from solid biomass_CL2_ biomass from MSW, combustion and waste-to-energy, at plant</baseName>
      </name>
      <common:synonyms>Energia elettrica da biomasse solide _Cl2_biomasse da rifiuti solidi urbani (RSU), combustione e termovalorizzazione, all’impianto</common:synonyms>
      <classificationInformation>
        <common:classification name="ILCDCategories" classes="../ILCDClassification.xml">
          <common:class level="0">Energy carriers and technologies</common:class>
          <common:class level="1">Electricity</common:class>
        </common:classification>
      </classificationInformation>
      <common:generalComment>Dataset developed according to Arcadia project Methodology (Report: “Metodologia per gli studi di filiera della Banca Dati italiana LCA”). LCA study of electricity production from solid biomass  (Report: “La filiera delle biomasse solide  per la produzione di energia elettrica in Italia”). &#13;
The dataset refers to the production of 1 kWh (=3.6 MJ) of electricity from solid biomass derived from municipal solid waste (MSW), and it is representative of the processing technologies commonly used for this purpose.&#13;
</common:generalComment>
      <referenceToExternalDocumentation type="source data set" refObjectId="e27984c9-9c85-458b-beaa-c727f7127c3d" version="01.00.000" uri="../sources/e27984c9-9c85-458b-beaa-c727f7127c3d.xml">
        <common:shortDescription>Gabriella Fiorentino, Giuliana Ansanelli, Antonietta Cerbone, Alessandro Giocoli, Vincenzo Motola e Amalia Zucaro. LA FILIERA DELLE BIOMASSE SOLIDE PER LA PRODUZIONE DI ENERGIA ELETTRICA IN ITALIA.&#13;
&#13;
Background datasets from Ecoinvent database cut-off (v. 3.7.1) were used for the LCA study.&#13;
</common:shortDescription>
      </referenceToExternalDocumentation>
    </dataSetInformation>
    <quantitativeReference type="Reference flow(s)">
      <referenceToReferenceFlow>0</referenceToReferenceFlow>
    </quantitativeReference>
    <time>
      <common:referenceYear>2021</common:referenceYear>
      <common:dataSetValidUntil>2026</common:dataSetValidUntil>
      <common:timeRepresentativenessDescription>This dataset has been considered valid until 2026, since no main changes have occurred in the electricity production from solid biomass in the investigated years.</common:timeRepresentativenessDescription>
    </time>
    <geography>
      <locationOfOperationSupplyOrProduction location="IT"/>
    </geography>
    <technology>
      <technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>The dataset refers to a system that includes the transportation of biomass (secondary data) and the combustion of biowaste from MSW (primary data) in order obtain electrical energy. The power of the waste-to-energy (WtE) plants is between 1 and 70 MW. The primary data were provided by environmental declarations of plants distributed throughout the country, that use municipal solid waste as biomass to obtain electricity, from Atlaimpianti (https://www.gse.it/dati-e-scenari/atlaimpianti), and the GSE (Gestore Servizi Energetici), 2022. Statistical Report 2020 on Renewable Sources.&#13;
Background data were modelled according to EcoInvent database 3.7.1&#13;
</technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>
      <technologicalApplicability>Electricity from solid biomass sold to Italian electric grid.</technologicalApplicability>
      <referenceToTechnologyPictogramme type="source data set" refObjectId="cdb7c987-0e52-4eb6-9aa3-2966c0b6bd03" version="01.00.000" uri="../sources/cdb7c987-0e52-4eb6-9aa3-2966c0b6bd03.xml">
